{%- comment -%}
  Announcement + header, one section (header-group): hamburger + search left
  · wordmark centered · bag with count right. No account icon, no wishlist,
  no mega menu — the full category list lives in one paper overlay. The bar
  is fixed AND permanently frosted on every template and viewport (the base
  stylesheet's .hdr-wrap), and every body carries --chrome-h padding, so no
  content ever runs under it — a transparent-at-scroll-0 state and its
  theme.js class toggle are intentionally NOT used here (it made trust links,
  the hero caption and the PDP gallery unreadable/overlapping under the bar).
  Do not reintroduce.

  TWO-TIER: the top row shrinks to logo + search/bag + hamburger only; the
  categories move to a second row underneath, still inside .hdr-wrap so they
  stay part of the same fixed, frosted lid. `two_tier` is the kill switch
  back to the original single row (default ON) — the single-row branch below
  is the original markup, byte for byte, so turning it off is zero-risk.

  Growing the bar for the second row (and the optional third, quick-line) can't
  add a second hardcoded height number: the base stylesheet already computes
  --chrome-h: calc(--ann-h + --hdr-h), and body's top padding runs off that. So
  --hdr-h itself gets overridden from here, once, and --chrome-h just follows —
  see the <style> tag below instead of a duplicate constant in header-extras.css.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign menu = section.settings.menu | default: linklists['main-menu'] -%}
{%- assign menu_secondary = section.settings.menu_secondary -%}
{%- assign menu_trust = section.settings.menu_trust -%}
{%- comment -%} Desktop nav menu: the DESKTOP bar splits the main menu around
the logo (ceil(n/2) left, remainder right), while the mobile overlay keeps the
category menu from `menu`. Setting empty = the previous behaviour (first 5 of
`menu` left, trust links right), so the fallback path is byte-identical to
before. Two-tier ON reuses the SAME setting for the second row, just no
longer split around a logo that isn't in that row anymore — see the two_tier
branch below. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign menu_desktop = section.settings.menu_desktop -%}
{%- comment -%} floor(n/2) left, remainder right (Track Your Order belongs on
the right) — 5 links = Collections · Shop | Track Your Order · About us ·
Contact. Only used by the single-row (two_tier off) branch. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign desk_half = menu_desktop.links.size | divided_by: 2 -%}

{%- assign two_tier = section.settings.two_tier -%}
{%- assign menu_quickline = section.settings.menu_quickline -%}
{%- comment -%} The extra rows have to grow the body's top padding, and --chrome-h is
what the base stylesheet runs that padding off. But --chrome-h is NOT the thing to
compute a new absolute value for, and --hdr-h is NOT the thing to overwrite:

  --hdr-h: 56px          <- the TOP ROW's own height, not the total
  .hdr { height: var(--hdr-h) }
  --chrome-h: calc(var(--ann-h) + var(--hdr-h))
  @media … { --hdr-h: 68px; --ann-h: 30px }   <- desktop values
  (all defined in the base stylesheet)

Overwriting --hdr-h with the SUM (56+40) therefore did two things at once: it made the
top row itself 96px tall, and — because a plain :root rule in this section is later in
document order than the base stylesheet — it beat the desktop media query too. Net effect
at every width: real bar 32+96+40 = 168px, body padding only 32+96 = 128px, so 40px of
every page sat under the frosted lid.

So: leave --hdr-h alone, add ONLY the extra rows, and let --chrome-h keep deriving from
whatever --hdr-h and --ann-h are at the current breakpoint. calc() re-resolves per
breakpoint on its own, which is exactly why this stays one number in one place. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%} DESKTOP ONLY: the row is hidden below 721px in
header-extras.css, so its 40px must come out of the height budget at the same
breakpoint — otherwise every phone page keeps a 40px gap under the frosted
lid, which is the exact bug the comment above describes, just inverted. The
quick-line keeps its 32px on both widths; only the .hdr2 row is
desktop-bound. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign hdr_extra = 0 -%}
{%- assign hdr_extra_mobile = 0 -%}
{%- if two_tier -%}
  {%- assign hdr_extra = 40 -%}
  {%- if menu_quickline != blank -%}
    {%- assign hdr_extra = hdr_extra | plus: 32 -%}
    {%- assign hdr_extra_mobile = 32 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if hdr_extra > 0 -%}
  <style>:root{ --hdr-extra: {{ hdr_extra }}px; --chrome-h: calc(var(--ann-h) + var(--hdr-h) + var(--hdr-extra)); }
@media (max-width: 720px){ :root{ --hdr-extra: {{ hdr_extra_mobile }}px; } }</style>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="hdr-wrap">
  {%- comment -%} The merchant's announcement wins in every language. This used to
read the localized key on any non-primary locale, which discarded a merchant-typed
bar — and since the bar carries shipping and returns facts, it could advertise terms
the store never wrote. Blank stays blank: clearing the setting is how the bar is
turned off, so there is no locale fallback. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign hdr_ann = section.settings.announcement
-%}
{%- if hdr_ann != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%} ROTATING BAR: the same `·`-separated setting feeds one
    slide per fact instead of one long line. That also retires a width
    problem: the joined line can need 412px and wrap on a 390px phone — a
    single fact needs ~150px and always fits, at full letter-spacing.

    CSS-only, no JS: the track holds N slides and one keyframe animation steps it
    through them. Each slide gets an equal share of the cycle, so N facts × the
    per-slide dwell is the total duration; the Liquid below writes both numbers
    into the element so the CSS can stay generic. `prefers-reduced-motion` stops
    the animation on the first slide (see the base stylesheet) — the remaining
    facts are still in the DOM for screen readers, which is why this is not
    aria-hidden and not a live region: nothing is announced, the text is simply
    all there.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} The bundle offer joins the rotation as its own slide.

    GATED on settings.qty_tiers_enabled exactly like every other tier surface —
    with the switch off nothing is added, because a bar promising 10% that the
    checkout does not grant is the misrepresentation category that costs a
    Merchant Center account. The wording is BUILT from the first rung of
    settings.qty_tiers, so it can never drift from the ladder. Wording is a
    translation key with qty/pct params so every storefront language renders
    its own phrasing instead of hardcoded English. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign ann_source = hdr_ann -%}
    {%- if settings.qty_tiers_enabled and settings.qty_tiers != blank -%}
      {%- assign ann_first_tier = settings.qty_tiers | remove: ' ' | split: ',' | first | split: ':' -%}
      {%- if ann_first_tier.size == 2 -%}
        {%- capture ann_bundle_fact -%}{{ 'promo.bundle_slide' | t: qty: ann_first_tier[0], pct: ann_first_tier[1] }}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- assign ann_source = ann_source | append: ' · ' | append: ann_bundle_fact -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign ann_facts = ann_source | split: '·' -%}
    {%- assign ann_count = ann_facts.size -%}
    {%- assign ann_dwell = section.settings.announcement_dwell | default: 5 -%}
    {%- if ann_count > 1 -%}
      {%- assign ann_total = ann_dwell | times: ann_count -%}
      {%- comment -%} One hold + one slide per fact. The share of the cycle each
      fact owns is 100/N; it holds still for 82% of that share and travels during
      the remaining 18%. Emitted here because N is only known at render time. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign ann_share = 100.0 | divided_by: ann_count -%}
      {%- assign ann_hold = ann_share | times: 0.82 -%}
      <style>
        @keyframes ann-rotate {
          {%- for fact in ann_facts -%}
            {%- assign i = forloop.index0 -%}
            {%- assign at_start = ann_share | times: i | round: 3 -%}
            {%- assign at_hold = ann_share | times: i | plus: ann_hold | round: 3 -%}
            {{ at_start }}%, {{ at_hold }}% { transform: translateY(calc(var(--ann-h) * -{{ i }})); }
          {%- endfor -%}
          100% { transform: translateY(calc(var(--ann-h) * -{{ ann_count }})); }
        }
      </style>
      <div class="ann ann--rotating" style="--ann-slides: {{ ann_count }}; --ann-cycle: {{ ann_total }}s;">
        <div class="ann__track">
          {%- for fact in ann_facts -%}
            <p class="ann__slide">{{ fact | strip | escape }}</p>
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- comment -%} the first fact repeated as slide N+1 so the wrap-around
          scrolls onward instead of snapping back {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="ann__slide" aria-hidden="true">{{ ann_facts.first | strip | escape }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="ann">{{ hdr_ann | strip | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} no .wrap: the bar runs the FULL page width with only the gutter
  as padding — the base stylesheet's .hdr owns the padding. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if two_tier -%}
    <header class="hdr">
      <div class="hdr__side">
        <button type="button" class="hdr__icon hdr__burger" data-open-nav aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.open_menu' | t }}" aria-haspopup="dialog">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'menu', size: 22 %}
        </button>
      </div>

      <a class="hdr__logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }} home">
        {%- render 'logo-lockup' -%}
      </a>

      <div class="hdr__side hdr__side--end">
        {%- render 'loc-switcher', style: 'header' -%}
        <a class="hdr__icon" href="{{ routes.search_url }}" aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.search' | t }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'search', size: 20 %}
        </a>
        <button type="button" class="hdr__icon hdr__cart" data-open-cart aria-label="{{ 'header.cart.open_bag' | t: count: cart.item_count }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'cart', size: 20 %}
          <span class="cart-count" {% if cart.item_count == 0 %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </header>

    {%- comment -%} Second row: categories/pages as a slim line under the logo
    row, still inside .hdr-wrap so it's part of the same fixed frosted lid. Mobile
    scrolls sideways, desktop centres (header-extras.css) — same content either
    way, same fallback chain the old split-around-the-logo nav used, just no
    longer split (there's no logo in this row to split around). {%- endcomment -%}
    <nav class="hdr2 lbl" aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.primary' | t }}">
      <div class="hdr2__scroll">
        {%- if menu_desktop != blank -%}
          {%- for link in menu_desktop.links -%}
            <a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- for link in menu.links limit: 5 -%}
            <a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- if menu_trust != blank -%}
            {%- for link in menu_trust.links limit: 4 -%}
              <a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <a href="/pages/about-us">{{ 'header.nav.about_us' | t }}</a>
            <a href="/pages/faq">{{ 'header.nav.faq' | t }}</a>
            <a href="/pages/track-your-order">{{ 'header.nav.track_order' | t }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </nav>

    {%- comment -%} Category quick-line — a third, flatter row of bestseller
    categories. No setting = no row: --hdr-h above already didn't budget space
    for it, so there's nothing to leave an empty gap. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if menu_quickline != blank -%}
      <nav class="hdr-quick lbl-sm mute" aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.popular_categories' | t }}">
        <div class="hdr-quick__scroll">
          {%- for link in menu_quickline.links -%}
            <a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%} Single-row fallback (two_tier off) — untouched original
    markup, so switching the setting off is a zero-risk revert. {%- endcomment -%}
    <header class="hdr">
      <div class="hdr__side">
        <button type="button" class="hdr__icon hdr__burger" data-open-nav aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.open_menu' | t }}" aria-haspopup="dialog">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'menu', size: 22 %}
        </button>
        <a class="hdr__icon" href="{{ routes.search_url }}" aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.search' | t }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'search', size: 20 %}
        </a>
        <nav class="hdr__nav lbl" aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.primary' | t }}">
          {%- if menu_desktop != blank -%}
            {%- for link in menu_desktop.links limit: desk_half -%}
              <a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- for link in menu.links limit: 5 -%}
              <a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </nav>
      </div>

      <a class="hdr__logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }} home">
        {%- render 'logo-lockup' -%}
      </a>

      <div class="hdr__side hdr__side--end">
        {%- comment -%} Trust links right of the wordmark. A link_list is the
        override, but the default is hardcoded on purpose: adding a menu is a
        store-wide write, and this theme is read-only outside its own files. {%- endcomment -%}
        <nav class="hdr__nav hdr__nav--end lbl" aria-label="{{ 'header.nav.support' | t }}">
          {%- if menu_desktop != blank -%}
            {%- for link in menu_desktop.links offset: desk_half -%}
              <a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- elsif menu_trust != blank -%}
            {%- for link in menu_trust.links limit: 4 -%}
              <a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <a href="/pages/about-us">{{ 'header.nav.about_us' | t }}</a>
            <a href="/pages/faq">{{ 'header.nav.faq' | t }}</a>
            <a href="/pages/track-your-order">{{ 'header.nav.track_order' | t }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </nav>
        {%- render 'loc-switcher', style: 'header' -%}
        <button type="button" class="hdr__icon hdr__cart" data-open-cart aria-label="{{ 'header.cart.open_bag' | t: count: cart.item_count }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'cart', size: 20 %}
          <span class="cart-count" {% if cart.item_count == 0 %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </header>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- comment -%} Mobile-nav overlay: PARTIAL-width slide-in drawer, not a
full-bleed overlay. theme.js opens it unchanged from
[data-open-nav]/[data-close-dialog] — it is still the same
<dialog id="mobile-nav">, only header-extras.css draws it narrower and
sliding in from the left instead of full-screen. See that file for the
width/backdrop/animation overrides.

MULTI-LEVEL: native <details>/<summary> per level, so it needs ZERO
JavaScript and theme.js stays untouched.

History that still matters (do not reintroduce): this overlay used to FLATTEN
the whole tree into one directory list, because a "Shop" parent's children
were simply the same top-level categories again, printing five links twice.
The drill-down brings levels back, but keeps the anti-duplication rule that
fixed that bug — recursively, one level at a time: before turning a link into
an expander, check whether ITS children are themselves nothing but its own
siblings at that same level. If so, expanding it would show you a row you
already saw a second ago, so it renders as a plain link instead — never an
expander whose first (and only) reveal is a duplicate. `top_urls` is the
level-1 sibling set; `sib_urls` is the level-2 analogue, recomputed per parent
from that parent's OWN children, so a grandchild is checked against its real
siblings (the other children of the same parent) — not against level 1. {%- endcomment -%}
<dialog id="mobile-nav" class="menu" aria-label="{{ 'header.mobile.menu_aria' | t }}">
  <div class="menu__inner">
    <div class="menu__head">
      <span class="hdr__logo" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'logo-lockup' -%}</span>
      <button type="button" class="hdr__icon" data-close-dialog aria-label="{{ 'header.mobile.close_menu' | t }}">
        {% render 'icon', name: 'close', size: 22 %}
      </button>
    </div>

    <nav class="menu__list" aria-label="{{ 'header.mobile.categories' | t }}">
      {%- assign top_urls = '' -%}
      {%- for l in menu.links -%}
        {%- assign top_urls = top_urls | append: '|' | append: l.url | append: '|' -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- for link in menu.links -%}
        {%- assign link_has_unique = false -%}
        {%- assign sib_urls = '' -%}
        {%- for s in link.links -%}
          {%- assign sib_urls = sib_urls | append: '|' | append: s.url | append: '|' -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- capture link_panel -%}
          {%- for child in link.links -%}
            {%- assign child_key = '|' | append: child.url | append: '|' -%}
            {%- if top_urls contains child_key -%}
              {%- continue -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign link_has_unique = true -%}

            {%- assign child_has_unique = false -%}
            {%- capture child_panel -%}
              {%- for gc in child.links -%}
                {%- assign gc_key = '|' | append: gc.url | append: '|' -%}
                {%- if sib_urls contains gc_key -%}
                  {%- continue -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- assign child_has_unique = true -%}
                <a class="menu__sub-link" href="{{ gc.url }}">{{ gc.title | escape }}</a>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}

            {%- if child.links.size > 0 and child_has_unique -%}
              <details class="menu__item menu__item--sub">
                <summary class="menu__sub-link">
                  <span>{{ child.title | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="menu__expand" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', name: 'plus', size: 16 %}</span>
                </summary>
                <div class="menu__sub-panel menu__sub-panel--deep">
                  {%- comment -%} A parent that becomes a <summary> loses its own destination: the
            shopper can open its children but can no longer reach the parent collection
            itself. The "View all" row inside the panel gives it back, and it goes FIRST so
            it reads as the broadest option rather than an afterthought. {%- endcomment -%}
            <a class="menu__sub-link menu__view-all" href="{{ child.url }}">{{ 'header.mobile.view_all' | t: title: child.title }}</a>
                  {{ child_panel }}
                </div>
              </details>
            {%- else -%}
              <a class="menu__sub-link" href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}

        {%- if link.links.size > 0 and link_has_unique -%}
          <details class="menu__item">
            <summary class="menu__link">
              <span>{{ link.title | escape }}</span>
              <span class="menu__expand" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', name: 'plus', size: 18 %}</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="menu__sub-panel">
              <a class="menu__sub-link menu__view-all" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ 'header.mobile.view_all' | t: title: link.title }}</a>
              {{ link_panel }}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- else -%}
          <a class="menu__link" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </nav>

    <nav class="menu__sub lbl" aria-label="{{ 'header.mobile.secondary' | t }}">
      <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}">{{ 'header.mobile.search_link' | t }}</a>
      {%- if menu_secondary != blank -%}
        {%- for link in menu_secondary.links -%}
          <a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </nav>
    {%- render 'loc-switcher', style: 'menu' -%}
  </div>
</dialog>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Header",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "two_tier", "label": "Two-tier header", "info": "Top row (logo + search + bag + hamburger) plus a second row for categories/pages. Off = the original single row.", "default": true },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu", "label": "Menu", "default": "main-menu" },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_desktop", "label": "Category row", "info": "Two-tier on: the second header row (mobile scrolls sideways, desktop centres). Two-tier off: split around the logo like before (first half left, rest right). Empty = first 5 links of Menu, then Trust links. The overlay menu always uses Menu and supports its full depth (category → subcategory → deeper)." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_quickline", "label": "Category quick-line", "info": "Two-tier only. A third, flatter row of bestseller categories under the category row (e.g. Dresses · Sandals · Blouses & Tops). Empty = the row does not render." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_secondary", "label": "Secondary menu (overlay footer)", "info": "Help / about / contact links, shown small under the category list." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu_trust", "label": "Trust links", "info": "Fallback for the Category row when it's empty (two-tier), or the right-hand slot when two-tier is off. Empty = About us · FAQ · Track your order. Max 4 links." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "announcement", "label": "Announcement line", "info": "Rendered uppercase. Separate facts with · — each fact becomes one slide and they rotate automatically. A single fact (no ·) renders static.", "default": "Ships 1–3 workdays · Free shipping · 30-day returns" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "announcement_dwell", "label": "Seconds per announcement", "min": 3, "max": 10, "step": 1, "unit": "s", "default": 5 }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
